WEBVTT

00:00:13.723 --> 00:00:16.857
Vipera Evanesca.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.127
What are you
playing at?

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.097
You're
a Parselmouth?

00:00:40.097 --> 00:00:41.055
Why didn't you
tell us?

00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:42.143
I'm a what?

00:00:42.143 --> 00:00:43.144
You can talk to snakes.

00:00:43.144 --> 00:00:44.798
I know.

00:00:44.798 --> 00:00:47.670
I mean, I accidentally set
a python on my cousin, Dudley

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.411
at the zoo once.

00:00:49.411 --> 00:00:51.282
Once. But so what?

00:00:51.282 --> 00:00:53.546
I bet loads of people here
can do it.

00:00:53.546 --> 00:00:55.635
No, they can't.

00:00:55.635 --> 00:00:57.462
It's not a very common gift,
Harry.

00:00:57.462 --> 00:00:59.856
This is bad.

00:00:59.856 --> 00:01:01.554
What's bad?

00:01:01.554 --> 00:01:03.817
If I hadn't told that snake
not to attack Justin--

00:01:03.817 --> 00:01:05.122
Oh, that's what you said to it.

00:01:05.122 --> 00:01:06.123
You were there.

00:01:06.123 --> 00:01:07.255
You heard me.

00:01:07.255 --> 00:01:09.562
I heard you speaking
Parseltongue.

00:01:09.562 --> 00:01:11.651
Snake language.

00:01:11.651 --> 00:01:14.697
I spoke
a different language?

00:01:14.697 --> 00:01:18.353
But I didn't realize--

00:01:18.353 --> 00:01:20.703
How can I speak a language
without knowing I can?

00:01:20.703 --> 00:01:22.357
I don't know, Harry.

00:01:22.357 --> 00:01:24.533
But it sounded like
you were egging the snake on.

00:01:24.533 --> 00:01:27.101
Harry, listen to me.

00:01:27.101 --> 00:01:30.495
There's a reason the symbol
of Slytherin house is a serpent.

00:01:30.495 --> 00:01:33.455
Salazar Slytherin
was a Parselmouth.

00:01:33.455 --> 00:01:34.891
He could talk to snakes too.

00:01:34.891 --> 00:01:37.502
Exactly. Now the whole school
is going to think

00:01:37.502 --> 00:01:39.896
you're his great-great-great
grandson or something.

00:01:39.896 --> 00:01:41.245
But I'm not!

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.774
I can't be.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.993
He lived a thousand
years ago.

00:01:49.993 --> 00:01:52.953
For all we know,
you could be.

00:02:23.026 --> 00:02:25.289
I'll see you back
in the common room.

00:02:39.782 --> 00:02:41.828
Blood.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:45.222
I want blood.

00:02:45.222 --> 00:02:47.616
[♪♪♪]

00:02:49.183 --> 00:02:54.623
They all must die.

00:02:54.623 --> 00:02:57.234
Kill.

00:02:57.234 --> 00:03:00.107
Kill.

00:03:00.107 --> 00:03:02.849
Kill!

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:06.635
Time to kill.

00:03:40.756 --> 00:03:42.889
Caught in the act.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:45.239
I'll have you out
this time, Potter.

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:48.938
Mark my words.

00:03:48.938 --> 00:03:53.508
No, Mr. Filch.
You don't understand--

00:04:19.055 --> 00:04:20.056
Professor...

00:04:20.056 --> 00:04:22.842
I swear I didn't.

00:04:22.842 --> 00:04:24.974
This is out of my hands, Potter.

00:04:35.028 --> 00:04:37.770
Professor Dumbledore
will be waiting for you.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.781
Sherbet Lemon.

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.947
Professor Dumbledore?

00:05:42.269 --> 00:05:45.272
Bee in your bonnet, Potter?

00:05:47.883 --> 00:05:49.537
I was just wondering

00:05:49.537 --> 00:05:52.496
if you put me
in the right house.

00:05:52.496 --> 00:05:54.455
Yes...

00:05:54.455 --> 00:05:58.763
You were particularly
difficult to place,

00:05:58.763 --> 00:06:02.245
but I stand by
what I said last year.

00:06:02.245 --> 00:06:05.553
You would have done well
in Slytherin.

00:06:05.553 --> 00:06:07.076
You're wrong.

